PLR 3.3.2: stateful data descriptor. `c.x = 5` routes through Pos.__set__
(emit_descriptor_set), which stores obj._v; `c.x` routes through __get__,
which reads obj._v. The instance is boxed as a CLASS python_value
(coerce_to_typed_slot) so obj aliases c. Works because Holder (declaring
_v) is registered before the descriptor method bodies convert.
